/T (This question again provided a good number of marks for the vast majority of candidates, who showed an adequate knowledge of integration, but in an unexpectedly large number  of cases sign errors were made in part \(a\), causing the letters p and q to be interchanged.  In part \(b\), most candidates were able to identify correctly which integral had the finite  value. )
/E (This question again provided a good number of marks for the vast majority of candidates, who showed an adequate knowledge of integration, but in an unexpectedly large number  of cases sign errors were made in part \(a\), causing the letters p and q to be interchanged.  In part \(b\), most candidates were able to identify correctly which integral had the finite  value. )
