/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Most candidates were able to integrate the given powers of x, and many were able to  draw the correct conclusions, though sign errors were common in part \(b\). In part \(c\), most of those who had been successful so far were able to complete the task successfully, but it was noticeable that some candidates did not take a hint from the award of only one mark for this part of the question: instead of drawing a quick conclusion from the results already obtained they went through the whole process of integrating, substituting and taking limits, possibly losing valuable time. )
/E (Most candidates were able to integrate the given powers of x, and many were able to  draw the correct conclusions, though sign errors were common in part \(b\). In part \(c\), most of those who had been successful so far were able to complete the task successfully, but it was noticeable that some candidates did not take a hint from the award of only one mark for this part of the question: instead of drawing a quick conclusion from the results already obtained they went through the whole process of integrating, substituting and taking limits, possibly losing valuable time. )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [11]
